{
 "about": "Every way to bring in a sound. bell: an installed plugin by name with one of its presets (the presets tool lists them). osc: a plugin by name with its format chosen, and no preset, so it arrives as FL would load it fresh (a fresh 3x Osc is a sine; 07 shapes it by automation). flex: the template's FLEX channel, as the template saved it. kick: a sampler holding a sample, so notes pitch it (C4 plays it as recorded). vocal: an audio clip, placed on the playlist and trimmed to [start_ms, end_ms]. Paths starting %FLStudioFactoryData% are FL's own packs, found on any install. One pattern holds notes for several instruments.",
